@startuml dependency_diagram

title Dependency Layers - Clean Architecture

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

package "Layer 1: Domain & Exceptions" {
    component "Task\nTaskComment\nProject\nTaskStatus" as Domain
    component "DomainError\nTaskNotFoundError\nCommentNotFoundError\nProjectNotFoundError\nImportExportError" as Exceptions
}

package "Layer 2: Storage Abstraction" {
    component "JsonStorage" as Storage
    component "StoragePathProvider" as PathProvider
}

package "Layer 3: Repository" {
    component "BaseRepository<T>" as BaseRepo
    component "TaskRepository\nCommentRepository\nProjectRepository" as Repositories
}

package "Layer 4: Services" {
    component "TodoService\nExportService\nImportService" as Services
}

package "Layer 5: Dependency Injection" {
    component "Container" as Container
}

package "Layer 6: CLI User Interface" {
    component "TodoCLI\nInteractiveMenu" as CLI
}

'' Layering arrows (dependencies point DOWN, never UP)
Domain .up.> Exceptions : uses

Storage .up.> PathProvider : uses

BaseRepo .down.> Storage : uses
Repositories .down.> BaseRepo : extends

Services .down.> Repositories : depends on
Services .down.> Exceptions : raises/handles

Container .down.> Services : creates
Container .down.> Repositories : creates
Container .down.> Storage : creates

CLI .down.> Container : uses
CLI .down.> Exceptions : handles

'' Cross-layer usage (exceptions cross all layers)
Repositories .down.> Exceptions : raises
Services .down.> Exceptions : raises
CLI .down.> Exceptions : catches

note bottom
    CLEAN DEPENDENCY GRAPH:

    Layer 6 (CLI) depends on Layer 5 (Container)
    Layer 5 (Container) depends on Layer 4 (Services)
    Layer 4 (Services) depends on Layer 3 (Repository)
    Layer 3 (Repository) depends on Layer 2 (Storage)

    ACYCLIC: No circular dependencies!

    INVERSION OF CONTROL:
    - CLI does not directly instantiate repositories
    - Services do not know about storage paths
    - Container manages all dependency wiring
    - Each layer has single responsibility
end note

@enduml
